---
// src/pages/snow.astro
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="UTF-8">
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
	<title>Interactive Snow Effect Tutorial - Step 1</title>
	<meta name="description" content="Learn how to build a high-performance interactive snow effect with HTML5 Canvas and vanilla JavaScript.">
	
	<!-- Google Fonts -->
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
	<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
	
	<style>
		:root {
			--bg-color: #030712;
			--panel-bg: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);
			--panel-border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
			--text-primary: #f3f4f6;
			--text-secondary: #9ca3af;
			--accent: #60a5fa;
			--accent-glow: rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.15);
		}

		* {
			box-sizing: border-box;
			margin: 0;
			padding: 0;
		}

		body {
			font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif;
			background-color: var(--bg-color);
			color: var(--text-primary);
			min-height: 100vh;
			overflow: hidden;
			position: relative;
		}

		/* Fullscreen Canvas for the Snow Effect */
		#snowCanvas {
			position: absolute;
			top: 0;
			left: 0;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			z-index: 1;
			background: radial-gradient(circle at center, #0b1528 0%, #030712 100%);
		}

		/* Educational Dashboard Overlay */
		.dashboard {
			position: absolute;
			top: 0;
			left: 0;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			z-index: 10;
			pointer-events: none; /* Let clicks pass through to canvas if needed */
			display: flex;
			flex-col: column;
			flex-direction: column;
			justify-content: space-between;
			padding: 2rem;
		}

		/* Top Navigation Header */
		header {
			pointer-events: auto;
			display: flex;
			justify-content: space-between;
			align-items: center;
			background: var(--panel-bg);
			backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
			border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
			padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
			border-radius: 16px;
			box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
			max-width: 1200px;
			width: 100%;
			margin: 0 auto;
		}

		.logo-area h1 {
			font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.5rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			letter-spacing: -0.02em;
			background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffffff 0%, #93c5fd 100%);
			-webkit-background-clip: text;
			-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
		}

		.step-badge {
			background: var(--accent-glow);
			border: 1px solid rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.3);
			color: var(--accent);
			padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
			border-radius: 9999px;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			font-weight: 600;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		}

		/* Bottom Control Panel & Code/Tutorial explanation */
		.tutorial-panel {
			pointer-events: auto;
			background: var(--panel-bg);
			backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
			border: 1px solid var(--panel-border);
			padding: 1.5rem;
			border-radius: 20px;
			box-shadow: 0 20px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
			max-width: 600px;
			width: 100%;
			margin: 0 auto;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 1rem;
			transition: all 0.3s ease;
		}

		.tutorial-panel h2 {
			font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
			font-size: 1.25rem;
			font-weight: 600;
			color: #ffffff;
		}

		.tutorial-panel p {
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			line-height: 1.6;
			color: var(--text-secondary);
		}

		.feature-list {
			list-style: none;
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 0.5rem;
			margin-top: 0.5rem;
		}

		.feature-list li {
			display: flex;
			align-items: center;
			gap: 0.5rem;
			font-size: 0.9rem;
			color: var(--text-primary);
		}

		.feature-list li::before {
			content: "❄";
			color: var(--accent);
		}

		.highlight {
			color: var(--accent);
			font-weight: 500;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>

	<!-- The drawing board for our snow effect -->
	<canvas id="snowCanvas"></canvas>

	<!-- Beautiful Dashboard Overlay -->
	<div class="dashboard">
		<header>
			<div class="logo-area">
				<h1>Let it Snow: Canvas Particle Tutorial</h1>
			</div>
			<div class="step-badge">Step 1: The Canvas Setup</div>
		</header>

		<div class="tutorial-panel">
			<h2>Step 1: Creating the Stage 🎬</h2>
			<p>
				Welcome! In this tutorial, we will build a beautiful, high-performance interactive snow effect from scratch. 
				Instead of using heavy libraries, we will write pure, clean <span class="highlight">HTML5 Canvas</span> and <span class="highlight">Vanilla JavaScript</span>.
			</p>
			<p>
				We have set up our workspace with:
			</p>
			<ul class="feature-list">
				<li>A full-screen <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code> element styled to cover the viewport.</li>
				<li>A radial gradient dark cosmic/arctic background that makes snow particles pop.</li>
				<li>A modern glassmorphic dashboard overlay for explanations and interactive controls.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Ready to see the code that initializes the canvas context and handles high-DPI screens?
			</p>
			<p style="font-weight: 600; color: #ffffff; text-align: center; margin-top: 0.5rem; border-top: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,0.1); padding-top: 0.5rem;">
				💬 Prompt <span class="highlight">"continue"</span> to progress to Step 2!
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

</body>
</html>
